5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run multichannel outbound sequences — email, phone, LinkedIn, and events — targeting technical buyers at OEMs across the DACH region</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use tools like Apollo, Clay, Lusha, and LinkedIn Sales Navigator to build and work targeted lead lists</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualify prospects through cold call sequences to identify ICP fit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hand off warm opportunities to Account Executives with clean notes and context</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track your own metrics and bring frontline market insights back to sales and marketing leadership</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Required BDR/SDR experience in B2B SaaS (or strong hunger to break in)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in German and English — you'll be reaching buyers across the DACH region</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with rejection and energized by outbound</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driven to grow into an Account Executive role and willing to earn it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus: experience or genuine curiosity in electronics, manufacturing, or hardware</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have: you use AI as more than a better search engine. Ideally you've built your own automations, workflows, or tools — we care about what you've actually shipped, not what you've read them</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work setup</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote from Germany. Munich is our global HQ; we also have a Berlin hub. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Travel</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We meet regularly for team retreats and selected industry events, so expect occasional travel. We cover the costs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Luminovo</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join a well-funded SaaS scaleup at a pivotal growth stage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear path to Account Executive with a team invested in your development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid in Munich or Berlin with an international, high-performance team</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>🤓 Whom you’ll be working with</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dasha-vyazemskaya/">Dasha</a>, our BDR Lead </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/cliftonlobo/">Clifton</a>, our VP Global Sales</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/inga-schwarz/">Inga</a>, our pioneer AE in the OEM market segment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/maxhungenbach/">Seba</a>, one of our founders, supporting the OEM GTM team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/maxhungenbach/">Max</a>, our Revenue Operations Team Lead, and his team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Product Managers, so you fully understand our product roadmap, potential constraints, and share product-related customer feedback</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>⚡️ Skills, knowledge, and expertise</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Just so you know – we purposefully did not create a standard list of minimum qualifications for this role. We care much more about your motivation and ability to help us accelerate technical progress than we care just about your CV. If you're interested to find out more about why we banned requirements from our performance profiles – see <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/startup-grind/why-we-banned-requirements-from-our-job-descriptions-33a774e1a1c2">here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>⚡️ About Luminovo</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Luminovo is the first electronics supply chain platform that unites all data, processes, and stakeholders in the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://luminovo.com/resources/blog/a-short-primer-on-the-electronics-industry?utm_campaign=employer_branding&amp;utm_source=candidate-traffic">trillion-dollar electronics industry</a>.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We fundamentally believe that technology is the best tool that humankind has developed to tackle the biggest challenges we face as a society today. And we want to do our share in accelerating technological progress. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>We bring innovations to life faster and cheaper by creating a more connected and resilient electronics supply chain.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, over 300 active customers worldwide are working with us towards this shared goal. Supported by leading investors such as Cherry Ventures, General Catalyst/LaFamiglia, Chalfen Ventures, and others, we have <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://luminovo.com/resources/blog/luminovo-raises-eu11-million-in-seed-funding-to-fix-the-broken-electronics-value-chain-with-transformative-software-suite">raised more than €20 million</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our core principles: putting people first &amp; building great things</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a remote-first company headquartered in Munich, our brilliant team is spread across cities including Munich, New York, Austin, Calgary, Berlin, London, Valencia, Nairobi, and Verona, among others. 🌍</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team includes a mix of product enthusiasts, people advocates, business masterminds, and engineering experts. Among us are graduates from institutions like Stanford University and the University of Cambridge, as well as talented individuals with unconventional CVs. What matters most is their drive to build great things.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We provide an authentic environment based on psychological safety to empower Luminerds from various backgrounds to succeed, grow, and focus on impact. Putting people first means that we deeply care about who our employees are, what makes them unique, and what they excel at. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">See what employees and candidates have to say about Luminovo on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.kununu.com/de/luminovo">kununu</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.de/Bewertungen/luminovo-ai-Bewertungen-E2039308.htm">Glassdoor</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><hr><p>Compensation: €64K – €110K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission • Multiple Ranges</p><ul><li>Germany | Level 1 • On-Target Earnings €64K – €68K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission</li><li>Germany | Level 2 • On-Target Earnings €77K – €89K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission</li><li>Germany | Level 3 • On-Target Earnings €100K – €110K • Offers Equity • Offers Commission</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/luminovo-gmbh/business-development-bdr-dach-remote-250782","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"🇪🇺 Germany (remote)","created_at":1792377615},{"slug":"head-of-growth-berlin-309647","company_name":"nara GmbH","title":"Head of Growth (m/w/d)","description":"<h2>Über nara</h2><p>nara erledigt die Arbeit, die in IT-Abteilungen jeden Tag anfällt. Mitarbeitende schreiben nara in Microsoft Teams oder rufen an. nara findet die Ursache und löst das Problem direkt in den Systemen, auf Servern und Geräten, vom Drucker, der nicht mehr druckt, bis zum Onboarding mit Konten, Zugängen und Software. Jedes Unternehmen legt selbst fest, was nara allein erledigt und wo ein Mensch freigibt.</p><p>Wir haben nara 2025 in Würzburg gegründet. Heute läuft nara produktiv bei Unternehmen aus Fertigung, Handel, Versicherung und IT-Services. Unsere Kunden sind Unternehmen ab etwa 1.000 Mitarbeitenden mit eigener IT-Abteilung sowie Managed Service Provider.</p><p>Das Produkt ist im Einsatz. Jetzt soll jede IT-Leitung in Deutschland nara kennen. Dafür suchen wir jemanden, der Growth komplett übernimmt, vom ersten Kontakt bis zum Termin, und im Vertrieb selbst mit anpackt.</p><h2>Die Rolle</h2><p>Du sorgst dafür, dass nara so schnell wie möglich wächst. Wie du das schaffst, entscheidest du.</p><p>Unser Vertrieb kümmert sich vor allem um Demos, Beziehungen und Abschlüsse. Alles davor liegt bei dir: Zielkunden finden, Kampagnen aufsetzen, Entscheider ansprechen, Gespräche vereinbaren. Du bist aber auch Teil des Vertriebs, führst eigene Termine und unterstützt, wo es nötig ist. Ein Marketingteam und feste Prozesse gibt es noch nicht, die baust du mit uns auf.</p><p>Dein Ziel: So viele qualifizierte Termine für unseren Vertrieb wie möglich, jeden Monat mehr als im Monat davor. Daran messen wir dich.</p><h2>Deine Aufgaben</h2><ul><li><p>Du findest heraus, über welche Wege wir IT-Leiter und Entscheider in unseren Zielunternehmen am besten erreichen.</p></li><li><p>Du sprichst sie selbst an, am Telefon, auf LinkedIn, per E-Mail oder persönlich.</p></li><li><p>Du wählst Messen und Events aus und sorgst dafür, dass wir von dort mit konkreten Gesprächen zurückkommen.</p></li><li><p>Du setzt Kampagnen online und offline auf, misst, was funktioniert, und stellst ab, was nicht funktioniert.</p></li><li><p>Du entwickelst gemeinsam mit uns die Website und unsere Inhalte weiter, damit Interessenten auch von selbst auf uns zukommen, zum Beispiel über Webinare.</p></li><li><p>Du führst eigene Termine und übergibst qualifizierte Gespräche an unseren Vertrieb, mit dem du eng zusammenarbeitest.</p></li><li><p>Wenn der Bereich wächst, baust du ein Team auf.</p></li></ul><h2>Was du mitbringst</h2><ul><li><p>Du hast mindestens einmal etwas von null zum Laufen gebracht: einen Kanal, ein Nebenprojekt, ein eigenes Geschäft oder einen Bereich in einem frühen Startup. Du kannst Zahlen dazu nennen.</p></li><li><p>Du hast im B2B-Bereich Leads generiert und weißt, woran man einen guten Termin von einem schlechten unterscheidet.</p></li><li><p>Du telefonierst gern, auch kalt.</p></li><li><p>Du arbeitest selbstständig und triffst Entscheidungen, ohne auf Anweisungen zu warten.</p></li><li><p>Du setzt Tools und Automatisierung ein, wo sie dich schneller machen.</p></li><li><p>Du kennst die Regeln für Kaltakquise in Deutschland (UWG, DSGVO) und hältst dich daran.</p></li><li><p>Du sprichst und schreibst fließend Deutsch und gut Englisch.</p></li><li><p>Erfahrung im B2B-Softwarevertrieb ist von Vorteil, idealerweise im ITSM-Umfeld oder mit IT-Abteilungen und Managed Service Providern als Kunden. Ein Muss ist das nicht.</p></li><li><p>Du benutzt AI nicht nur um Emails oder Nachrichten verfassen zu lassen sondern zur vollen Automatisierung.</p></li></ul><h2>Was du wissen solltest</h2><ul><li><p>Es gibt keine klassische Einarbeitung, du startest direkt.</p></li><li><p>Am Anfang hast du kein eigenes Team und setzt vieles selbst um, in enger Abstimmung mit uns und unserem Vertrieb.</p></li><li><p>Du bekommst keine täglichen Aufgaben vorgegeben, sondern ein Ziel.</p></li><li><p>Als Startup ändern sich bei uns Prioritäten schnell, und vieles ist noch nicht dokumentiert.</p></li></ul><h2>Was wir bieten</h2><ul><li><p>Festgehalt von 70.000 bis 90.000 Euro brutto im Jahr, je nach Erfahrung</p></li><li><p>Mitarbeiterbeteiligungsprogramm</p></li><li><p>Volle Verantwortung für den Growth-Bereich ab dem ersten Tag</p></li><li><p>Freie Einteilung deiner Arbeitszeit, hybrid in Würzburg oder komplett remote</p></li><li><p>Budget für Tools, Kampagnen und Messen, über das du mitentscheidest</p></li><li><p>Direkter Draht zu allen Entscheidern</p></li></ul><h2>So bewirbst du dich</h2><p>Wir halten den Prozess kurz.</p><ul><li><p>Du schickst uns deinen Lebenslauf und ein paar Zeilen dazu, was du bisher aufgebaut hast, am besten mit Zahlen. Ein klassisches Anschreiben brauchen wir nicht.</p></li><li><p>Wir lernen uns in einem ersten Gespräch per Video kennen.</p></li><li><p>Im zweiten Gespräch triffst du die Gründer, gern auch vor Ort in Würzburg.</p></li><li><p>Danach entscheiden wir innerhalb weniger Tage.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/nara-gmbh/head-of-growth-berlin-309647","tags":["Remote","Management","Team Leader"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","teamleitung"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792377087},{"slug":"senior-regional-services-partner-emea-central-373909","company_name":"Elastic","title":"Senior Regional Services Partner - EMEA Central","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Elastic, the Search AI Company, enables everyone to find the answers they need in real time, using all their data, at scale — unleashing the potential of businesses and people. The Elastic Search AI Platform, used by more than 50% of the Fortune 500, brings together the precision of search and the intelligence of AI to enable everyone to accelerate the results that matter. By taking advantage of all structured and unstructured data — securing and protecting private information more effectively — Elastic’s complete, cloud-based solutions for search, security, and observability help organizations deliver on the promise of AI.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is The Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Elastic is seeking an experienced Regional Services Partner to lead our Enterprise Sector Services business in the EMEA Central region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of commercial ownership, customer engagement, and delivery excellence. You will be responsible for driving services bookings growth across federal, state, and regulated public institutions while ensuring successful execution of a portfolio of complex engagements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Regional Services Leader, you will partner closely with Enterprise Sector Account Executives, Solution Architects, Delivery teams, and Customer Success to define and execute tailored services strategies that accelerate time to value and drive long-term adoption of Elastic solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role means consistently achieving Services bookings and revenue targets while delivering predictable, high-quality outcomes for Enterprise Sector customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and achieve Services bookings and revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute a territory services strategy aligned with account plans and long-term adoption objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate forecasting and proactively manage pipeline gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the services bid and negotiation lifecycle, including scope, pricing, contract structures, and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive discovery and shape outcome-oriented services offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop compelling Statements of Work tied to measurable milestones and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position Elastic Services as a strategic enabler for transformation initiatives within Enterprise&amp;nbsp; Sector organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee a portfolio of concurrent engagements, ensuring delivery within cost, margin, and customer satisfaction expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide governance oversight for strategic accounts, managing escalations and aligning Sales, Delivery, and Customer Success stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and mitigate risks, facilitate steering meetings, and ensure structured reporting and change management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic advisor, aligning Elastic Services to customer mission objectives and regulatory constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively within a matrixed organization across Sales, Delivery, Operations, and Partner teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in Professional Services, program delivery, or pre-sales roles within enterprise technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience working with Enterprise Sector organizations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven commercial ownership of services bookings targets, including forecasting and complex contract negotiations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in delivering technology solutions in search, observability, analytics, or security domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing multiple concurrent engagements with governance and risk oversight responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in German and English required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 50% (and occasionally internationally).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Elasticsearch and related technologies (Linux, NoSQL, distributed systems).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP, PRINCE2, or Scrum Master certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a billable consultant or project manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain SU2 security clearance if required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-PF1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Information - We Take Care of Our People&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a distributed company, diversity drives our identity. Whether you’re looking to launch a new career or grow an existing one, Elastic is the type of company where you can balance great work with great life. Your age is only a number. It doesn’t matter if you’re just out of college or your children are; we need you for what you can do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to have parity of benefits across regions and while regulations differ from place to place, we believe taking care of our people is the right thing to do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive pay based on the work you do here and not your previous salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage for you and your family in many locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to craft your calendar with flexible locations and schedules for many roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous number of vacation days each year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase your impact - We match up to $2000 (or local currency equivalent) for financial donations and service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 40 hours each year to use toward volunteer projects you love&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embracing parenthood with minimum of 16 weeks of parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Different people approach problems differently. We need that. Elastic is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to creating an inclusive culture that celebrates different perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, disability status, or any other basis protected by federal, state or local law, ordinance or regulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome individuals with disabilities and strive to create an accessible and inclusive experience for all individuals. To request an accommodation during the application or the recruiting process, please email &lt;a ----- ----- class=&quot;gmail_default&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;We will reply to your request within 24 business hours of submission.&lt;/p&gt;
