&lt;p&gt;Please see&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.elastic.co/legal/applicant-privacy-statement&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.elastic.co/legal/applicant-privacy-statement&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1611068262479000&amp;amp;usg=AFQjCNG3orAPk5sJIr9WVm0ZDxYw82c5DA&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for our Privacy Statement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/elastic/senior-regional-services-partner-emea-central-373909","tags":["Consulting - EMEA"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792367721},{"slug":"full-stack-software-engineer-react-typescript-python-django-hamburg-388907","company_name":"Mindpeak","title":"Full-Stack Software Engineer (React, TypeScript, Python/Django)","description":"<h1><strong>Company Overview</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Mindpeak is a Hamburg-based AI company dedicated to democratizing cancer diagnostics. Our software supports pathologists in detecting cancer faster and more accurately by applying state-of-the-art deep learning to medical images. Our AI solution is the first to be implemented in clinical histopathology for primary diagnostics in the USA and is used in routine workflows around the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We tackle a central challenge in modern healthcare: a growing demand for medical image analysis with a static number of cancer experts. By providing powerful, robust tools for visual diagnosis, we help pathologists focus on what only humans can do best—while our technology takes care of the rest.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h1><strong>Position Summary</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role</strong>: Fullstack Developer (TypeScript/JavaScript, React, OpenLayers, Python, Django, Postgres)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Focus</strong>: Building modern web UIs for AI-assisted pathology workflows, including their backend. Managing and maintaining our huge annotation data platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team</strong>: Close collaboration with product design, machine learning teams and annotators.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you'll work on</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build and optimize intuitive user interfaces</strong> for visualizing complex medical imaging data and AI-generated results, including millions of cell-level predictions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn complex AI outputs into clear, actionable insights</strong> for pathologists and other medical experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Develop tools and lightweight interfaces</strong> that simplify data collection, annotation, and review workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design, build, and integrate backend APIs</strong> that connect AI models with our applications, ensuring performance, reliability, and scalability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape and improve product features</strong> through close collaboration with pathologists, product teams, and designers, turning real-world feedback into practical solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Your Responsibilities</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ship high-quality features, from prototype to production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve performance, accessibility, and reliability of complex visualizations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own parts of the annotation pipeline UI and help automate repetitive steps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage priorities and deadlines in an agile environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate across teams to make scalable, user-centered product decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Your Profile</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education:</strong> Master's degree in Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience:</strong> 3+ years of experience developing production-ready web applications with a proven track record of delivering impactful features.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Frontend:</strong> Strong proficiency in TypeScript/JavaScript; experience with React is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Backend:</strong> Solid experience with Python and Django.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical skills:</strong> Familiarity with Linux and Docker is an advantage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong> Experience with OpenLayers, data-intensive user interfaces, Canvas, WebGL, D3.js, or frontend performance optimization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ways of working:</strong> Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, a collaborative mindset, and the ability to take ownership and work independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Curiosity:</strong> Interest in medical technology and a willingness to learn about digital pathology and laboratory workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Languages:</strong> Fluent English, both written and spoken.<br /></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div></li></ul><h1><strong>What Mindpeak Offers</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to bring cancer diagnostics to a whole new level and make a real impact on patient care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An open, creative work environment with flat hierarchies and quick decision-making.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close collaboration with a skilled, international team and experienced management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diverse, engaging projects that help you deepen both your technical and domain expertise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A centrally located Hamburg office with a beautiful view over the harbor.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div></li></ul><h1><strong>Application Details</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Please send us:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CV</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">University certificates and transcripts of records</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Job references</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Salary expectations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earliest possible starting date</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Contact:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Email: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ---------- style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Note:</strong> Direct applicants only. We do not work with recruiting agencies for this position.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mindpeak/full-stack-software-engineer-react-typescript-python-django-hamburg-388907","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hamburg","created_at":1792366832},{"slug":"workplace-experience-manager-munich-176327","company_name":"Proxima Fusion GmbH","title":"Workplace Experience Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO WE ARE</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Proxima Fusion, we're driven by a bold mission – to redefine the future of sustainable energy. Our unique concept, built upon the groundbreaking W7-X stellarator and the latest advances in technology, paves the way for commercially viable fusion power plants.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What’s more, our work in stellarator optimization, powered by cutting-edge computation and machine learning, is propelling us into uncharted territories of fusion technology. New higher performance design points are unlocked by high temperature superconducting magnets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To fully grasp this huge opportunity, we’re building a team of extremely dedicated and passionate people who come together driving something extraordinary, radically transforming technology in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHY JOIN PROXIMA FUSION</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will get to work on some of the most complex tech challenges to bring abundant, safe, clean energy to the world.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll get to join and learn from an exceptional selection of accomplished and driven individuals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do your life’s best work and enjoy the journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get to show that big things are possible in Europe when you assemble the best talent.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>YOUR IMPACT</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Workplace Experience Manager, you will own how it feels to work at Proxima across Munich, Oxford, Zurich and the sites still to come. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll lead our office managers, set one standard for the workplace experience, and work with Security, Operations and IT so every site runs smoothly, new ones included. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role suits someone who builds structure where there isn't any yet and cares about the details people notice. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As we grow across countries, you'll shape the spaces and rituals that make Proxima feel like one company, wherever our people sit.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT YOU WILL DO</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the workplace experience across Munich, Oxford, Zurich and future sites, setting one shared standard and making sure every location delivers on it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and develop the office management team, setting clear priorities and service levels so the sites run as one team, not three separate offices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launch new sites, owning fit-out input, vendor setup and local processes so each new office reaches standard quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the single point of contact between Security, Operations and IT on anything that affects employees' day-to-day: access, equipment, safety and space.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Standardise processes, policies and tools, so employees get the same answers and service levels wherever they work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the workplace budget and vendors across sites, balancing consistency with cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gather employee feedback through pulse checks and site walk-throughs, and turn it into concrete improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape culture through space and rituals, partnering with People on events, onboarding moments and community-building so the offices actively support how teams work together.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO YOU ARE</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly organized with strong attention to detail</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reliable, structured, and comfortable handling recurring administrative tasks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear and professional communicator in English (German is a plus)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working with Google Workspace, Slack, and other productivity tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discreet and trustworthy when handling sensitive information</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactive and service-oriented, with a “can-do” mindset</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>INTERVIEW PROCESS</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruiter interview (30-60 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring Manager interview (30-45 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team interviews (2x60 min)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">*This role sits at "LvL 2 out of 6" of our framework, please inquire during the recruitment process for further information.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Proxima Fusion, our mission is bold: making limitless clean energy a reality. To get there, we need a high-performing, diverse team that brings different perspectives, challenges assumptions, and builds together with purpose. We know that diversity of thought and experience leads to better ideas, stronger execution, and a more resilient team. We don’t look at how you identify, what you look like, who you choose to worship or what ethnicity you are. We care about what you can bring to the table.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/proxima-fusion-gmbh/workplace-experience-manager-munich-176327","tags":["People & Workplace Experience"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792366832},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-intern-all-genders-munich-452184","company_name":"Lio","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer Intern (all genders)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re not just writing code, you’re owning enterprise-scale implementations. You ensure Lio runs flawlessly in complex environments while building scalable, high-quality solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What You'll Do</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and extend enterprise integrations (e.g., SAP, APIs) in complex system landscapes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debug and resolve integration-heavy issues in live customer environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own customer-driven product features end-to-end</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop MVPs for new capabilities and evolve them into scalable platform solutions </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bridge short-term customer needs with long-term product architecture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automate and improve implementation workflows in collaboration with Product and Engineering</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Your Profile</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re a good fit for this role if you: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a background in Computer Science, Business Informatics, or similar</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring strong coding fundamentals and experience with APIs and system integrations </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understand enterprise architectures, data flows, and distributed systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy working at the intersection of engineering, product, and real customer environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are pragmatic, ownership-driven, and motivated by shipping high-impact solutions</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Why Join Us?</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Lio, you’ll work on cutting-edge AI in enterprise procurement, solving real SAP and integration challenges that directly shape our product roadmap. You’ll build features that matter, operate with high ownership, and move fast in an environment where impact is visible. Are you in?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have questions about the role? Feel free to reach out to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/gabriel-koch-executive-search/">Gabriel</a>!</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/lio/forward-deployed-engineer-intern-all-genders-munich-452184","tags":["Implementation"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Munich Office","created_at":1792366831},{"slug":"founders-associate-it-automation-munich-356060","company_name":"Lio","title":"Founders Associate (IT & Automation)","description":"<h2>Your Role at Lio</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Lio, we’re building a fast-growing AI company and we want our internal operations to reflect the technology we build.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Founder’s Associate Intern/ Working Student focused on IT &amp; Automation, you’ll own our day-to-day IT operations and build the systems that help us scale. You’ll make sure people have the tools, access, and support they need, then look for ways to make those processes simpler, more reliable and increasingly automated.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">One day, you might be setting up laptops, onboarding a new colleague, or troubleshooting our office network. The next, you could be connecting systems through APIs, building an internal tool or creating an AI agent that saves the team hours of manual work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make it work. Make it better. Then automate it.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work closely with our CTO, own projects from problem to implementation and see the impact of your work across the company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Everyday IT operations.</strong> Manage onboarding and offboarding, configure devices and accounts, resolve day-to-day IT issues, and keep our office network running reliably.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build IT that scales.</strong> Improve how we manage SaaS tools, access permissions, and device security, creating clear processes that grow with the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn repetitive work into automated workflows.</strong> Find manual tasks across IT and business operations, identify where automation adds value, and build solutions that save time and reduce errors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build practical internal tools.</strong> Use AI-assisted coding, Python, APIs, and low-code platforms to solve real operational problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Connect our systems.</strong> Integrate Microsoft 365, Slack, and other SaaS platforms so information flows smoothly and teams spend less time switching between tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Put AI to work.</strong> Test AI agents and emerging automation tools, turning useful experiments into reliable solutions the team can use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive improvements with the founders.</strong> Identify bottlenecks, propose a better approach, and take ownership of delivering it from the first idea through rollout and ongoing improvement.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why Join Lio?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lio is backed by <strong>Andreessen Horowitz (a16z)</strong> and built at <strong>Y Combinator</strong>. We're bringing Silicon Valley ambition and engineering culture to Munich.</p><p style="min-he