&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bitwarden/remote-principal-implementation-engineer-customer-support-16446","tags":["Customer Support"],"job_types":[],"location":"Remote","created_at":1792356936},{"slug":"revenue-operations-associate-london-222630","company_name":"Omnea","title":"Revenue Operations Associate","description":"<h2><strong>Our Mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Omnea, we’re reinventing how enterprise businesses operate, starting with the most painful parts: <strong>procurement</strong> – where a single purchase can drag on for months, trigger <strong>50+ emails</strong>, and pull in <strong>Finance, Legal, Security, and IT</strong> just to get something approved.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve raised <strong>$75M from Khosla Ventures, Insight Partners, </strong>and <strong>Accel </strong>to change that. Our AI-native platform connects every person, step, and system so buying is fast, safe, and efficient – one place to request, automated approvals and renewals, real-time supplier risk, and complete spend visibility. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity is massive. <strong>Every enterprise on the planet has this problem and nobody has solved it</strong>. We’ve 10x’d ARR to double-digit millions in 18 months and are trusted by global enterprises like Spotify, MongoDB, Monzo, and Albertsons. We’re now the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="c-link" href="https://sifted.eu/leaderboards/sifted-future-50-2025"><strong><u>4th fastest growing startup</u></strong></a> in Europe &amp; the Sunday Times' #1 Best Medium Sized Tech Company To Work for.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our team previously scaled Tessian</strong> (<strong>cybersecurity tech, </strong>backed by Sequoia, Balderton, Accel<strong>, </strong>acquired post-Series C), and our team includes ex-founders operators who’ve grown unicorns, shipped world-class products, and executed at the highest levels. You’ll work alongside leaders like <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="c-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ben-freeman-a8542166/"><strong><u>Ben</u></strong></a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="c-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/abhirukt/"><strong><u>Abs</u></strong></a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="c-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/scastiglione/"><strong><u>Sabrina</u></strong></a>, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="c-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rebecatristan/"><strong><u>Rebe</u></strong></a>.<br /></p><h2><strong>Find out more about the team and life at Omnea </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLpjeHyocsu3ZoDn3sfODjqIR2L_DW3dgb"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>. </strong></h2><h2>What we're looking for</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for someone hungry to learn and early in their career to join us as our <strong>Revenue Operations Associate</strong>!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You'll get an inside look at, and be a key part of, how a high-performing GTM function operates:</strong> this is a great opportunity for exceptionally smart, motivated individuals who want to immerse themselves in the world of tech startups and gain real exposure to what it takes to keep a high-growth business moving.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll sit at the intersection of our GTM, Customer and Finance teams, keeping our systems, data, and reporting sharp as we scale. This isn't a "keep the lights on" role – you'll inherit processes that are still being built, and you'll have real room to audit what's working, fix what isn't, and put your own stamp on how we operate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll get broad exposure early: one week you might be untangling a HubSpot workflow, the next you're building a dashboard the CCO takes into a board meeting. It's a genuinely excellent grounding in how a B2B SaaS business scales – but it comes with real pace, longer hours than a typical first job, and a learning curve to match. If you want breadth of exposure and a steep climb early in your career, this is a great seat.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What Can You Expect?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep our GTM tech stack in good shape:</strong> Own day-to-day CRM administration – data hygiene, permissions, and workflow upkeep – and support the configuration and integration of the wider stack.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay ahead of what's new:</strong> Keep across releases and new features across our tools – joining release webinars, reading release notes, and flagging what's worth adopting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Help evaluate and set up new tools:</strong> Get involved as we add to the stack, from evaluation through to implementation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve our data quality:</strong> Spot where data is incomplete or inconsistent, fix what you can, and propose fixes for the rest.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build reporting and dashboards:</strong> Turn raw data into dashboards and reports that track pipeline health, funnel conversion, and the other KPIs the GTM team relies on day to day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support incentive tracking:</strong> Help maintain and monitor commission and incentive tracking, making sure calculations are accurate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Onboard new GTM joiners:</strong> Train new starters across the GTM and Customer teams on our tools and processes so they're productive quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own our recurring admin cadence:</strong> Take ownership of the regular tasks that keep the engine running and look to automate where ever possible.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About You</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You have a top-class academic record:</strong> you'll have graduated with (or be on track for) a 1st class degree, or have attended one of the top universities in the country you studied in – we're looking for a strong, proven track record of academic performance as the clearest early signal of the analytical rigour this role needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You're curious about how technology fits together:</strong> you likely have a STEM background, and you enjoy working out how systems, data, and workflows connect to make a business run – even if you've never worked in RevOps before.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You want pace, eyes open:</strong> you're drawn to a fast-scaling business precisely because of the pace, and you understand that means longer hours and a steeper learning curve than a typical grad role. You see that as a trade worth making.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You're happy to get stuck in:</strong> you know not every task here is glamorous – some of it is spreadsheet clean-up, data hygiene, or repetitive admin – and you take real satisfaction in doing that work well, not just the exciting parts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You want to understand how B2B SaaS businesses scale:</strong> you're looking to build a first-hand understanding of the GTM engine – pipeline, systems, data, and the commercial mechanics behind it – as a foundation for wherever your career goes next.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Omnea, we embrace diversity. To build a product that's loved by everyone, we're best served by a team with all sorts of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We encourage you to apply even if your experience doesn't quite match the full job spec! And regardless of your race, religion, colour, gender, or anything else! If you think you could be a good fit for Omnea, please reach out.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>A few things to note: </strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer competitive geo-localised benefits, and you can check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/omnea/UK-Benefits-at-Omnea-36c88cce658781c39d08ee947693506f"><strong>UK Benefits Package</strong> here</a> and our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/omnea/US-Benefits-at-Omnea-36c88cce658781b49890e725794c0af1"> <strong>US Benefits Package</strong> here</a>. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work Tuesdays, Wednesdays &amp; Thursdays in-person at our offices. At this early stage of our company life-cycle it's important to us that we get this together-time, and you can read more about why we believe this is a winning move <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.omnea.co/documents/why-omnea-is-not-fully-remote">here</a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're commercial, ambitious and we don't pretend otherwise! We're actively seeking folks looking to make the most of a career-defining opportunity, with the hunger to be part of building something really <strong>impressive</strong>. You can see our values <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.omnea.co/careers">here</a> and our Omnea Future Founder's fund <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://news.crunchbase.com/startups/omnea-funding-employees-future-founders-freeman/">here</a>!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We sometimes use AI note-takers to help us transcribe interview notes, so we can be more present in your interview. If you'd like to opt out of us using automatic transcribers, please note this in the free text field in your application, otherwise we'll take your application as confirmation that you're happy for us to use notetakers (whether added to video calls or in the background).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are proud to be recognised for both our culture and product, and we are just getting started. Join us as we grow!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/aabd8e71-1f63-4593-a3bd-fb92bb6599c3/92866690-4282-4634-9428-2e0a6a4636db/new-ashby-banner.png" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>Legal note: if you are viewing this posting outside of the Omnea careers' page, this may be an auto-generated advertisement and may lack the full range of advertised information - please click through to the posting at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/omnea">https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/omnea</a> to view additional advertised information on this posting. <br />Additionally, where roles have hard-specified requirements (e.g. [x] days in office, unable to provide visas, etc), if in your application you provide deterministic check-box confirmation that you do not meet the hard-specified requirements, deterministic (not AI or subjective) automatic rejection criteria are in place.</h3><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/omnea/revenue-operations-associate-london-222630","tags":["Go To Market"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792356031},{"slug":"technical-delivery-manager-public-sector-london-259986","company_name":"Altanaai","title":"Technical Delivery Manager, Public Sector","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Altana is the network for trusted trade. Our AI-powered product network empowers governments and businesses to build a more resilient and secure global economy while keeping trade flowing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity at Altana&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a dedicated Technical Delivery Manager (TDM) who will have the exciting opportunity to collaborate closely with our public sector customers, guiding them in effectively and efficiently operating Altana’s platform. As a TDM, you’ll be the driving force behind user adoption, product enablement, and value realisation, ensuring overall customer success. You’ll be our customers’ champion, serving as their day-to-day relationship manager, conducting regular check-ins, and helping their end users consistently translate product insights into operational value.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Internally, you’ll articulate recurring customer needs and pain points to the business, wrangle cross-functional engineering and product teams to deliver on planned deliverables for your user base, and develop account strategies to strengthen our ongoing partnership with customers. You’ll evolve into a power use of Altana’s products and will use this knowledge to stimulate growth of product usage, up-selling, and cross-selling expansions. You will own the success of our customer deployments, focusing heavily on value creation and customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage successful customer deployments and technical work streams from end-to-end, with the ability to effectively manage priorities, deliver on-time, and communicate effectively internally and with customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become a power-user of the Atlas platform, then support Public Sector customers in rapidly achieving value, while identifying new use cases to address customer pain points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own customer relationships including conducting Quarterly Business Reviews and leveraging data-driven insights to astonish our clients while promptly relaying valuable feedback to the appropriate Altana teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to user support queries and build processes that enable us to scale our TAM functions as our customer base increases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be held accountable for effectively synthesising and communicating feedback to the product team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate the specification of new or expanded features, involving deep collaboration with Altana’s Product &amp;amp; Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our Implementation Engineering team to ensure successful delivery and work closely with our Sales Engineering team to identify and prioritise growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Account Executives to identify and capitalise on expansion opportunities, transforming them into reality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance strategic thinking with tactical execution, connecting day-to-day account management with broader commercial and product goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow to become an expert in how governments and enterprises can leverage technology to address supply chain risk, trade enforcement and trade facilitation use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 4-6 years of customer management, technology consulting, or general technology delivery experience, ideally some that involves working with government stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are just as comfortable working with software engineers and data scientists as you are with non-technical customer stakeholders, and have previous experience of translating complex data or technology concepts to new audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can demonstrate a history of successfully expanding technical accounts year over year or leading complex software projects and programmes to successful outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your ability to establish positive relationships and influence others is a key asset, complemented by excellent communication and interpersonal skills, balancing approachability with persistence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re open to feedback and thrive on cross-functional collaboration to drive continuous improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You exhibit good judgement and a willingness to dive into the nitty-gritty to achieve team objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are eligible and willing to obtain a UK Security Check (SC) clearance or have an active clearance already.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An active UK Security Check (SC) clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with public sector customers in the UK and overseas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the supply chain or logistics industry is a plus, although not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting self-directed data analysis to answer questions, ideally using SQL or similar languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in London with hybrid work flexibility and candidates must be within commuting distance from our Holborn office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recruiter assigned to this role can share more information about the specific compensation and benefit details associated with this role during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our values are the core beliefs that shape who we are, what we stand for, and how we behave.They form the foundation of Altana’s culture and integrity and guide how we hire, design, build, and connect with each other and our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trust:&lt;/strong&gt; Our customers and partners entrust us with missions of the highest importance. We honor that by keeping our word, meeting commitments, and ensuring every action we take reinforces confidence in us. We rely on each other to deliver, to speak openly, and to hold ourselves accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resilience: &lt;/strong&gt;In a world of uncertainty and complexity, our work must withstand challenges, evolve with conditions, and ensure reliability over time. Resilience is both how we operate and what we deliver. It’s how we respond when things don’t go to plan –– we adapt, we support each other, and we keep moving forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stewardship:&lt;/strong&gt; We are stewards of every mission we touch. Because our work impacts lives and futures, we hold ourselves accountable to delivering mission impact and never compromising. Our responsibility extends beyond individual projects to the broader system of global trade. We believe that stewardship starts from within so that we can bring focus, creativity, and excellence to our work. Each of us is personally responsible for fostering a workplace where people can thrive. And we are stewards of the greater good of the company. By holding ourselves and each other accountable, we build a culture of innovation and collective success that reflects the scale of our mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Courage: &lt;/strong&gt;Courage is what unlocks the seemingly impossible for our customers. It’s the core value that drives us make bold moves and take on big, complicated network problems—the ones others avoid. We know success isn&#39;t guaranteed, but we have the audacious vision to believe a solution is possible and to build it. Courage fuels our growth mindset. It means embracing challenges that make us stronger, and it’s demonstrated by how we approach hard conversations and complex projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Altana, we believe that a diverse workforce enables greater creativity, performance, and adaptability. We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and welcome you to join us as you are. Our employment opportunities and decisions are based on business needs and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religious creed, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, medical condition, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, family care or medical leave status, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by the laws or regulations in the areas in which we operate. We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any type, in any situation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Offers related to employment at Altana will come from an Altana.ai email address. We will never ask for payment as part of the interview or onboarding process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/altanaai/technical-delivery-manager-public-sector-london-259986","tags":["Sales and Delivery"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792346131},{"slug":"head-of-public-sector-business-development-national-security-london-143372","company_name":"Altanaai","title":"Head of Public Sector Business Development, National Security","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Altana is the network for trusted trade. Our AI-powered product network empowers governments and businesses to build a more resilient and secure global economy while keeping trade flowing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity at Altana&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Altana&#39;s Global Public Sector (GPS) team helps government customers work through hard problems in global trade and supply chains, and it&#39;s growing fast. As GPS scales, we&#39;re organizing around three domain verticals — Customs &amp;amp; Trade, Resilience &amp;amp; Network, and Policy &amp;amp; National Security — and we&#39;re hiring the founding Head of Policy &amp;amp; National Security to grow, manage, and run that business globally.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a foundational business development role&lt;/strong&gt; — a chance to build a business, not just join one. You&#39;ll own the growth of Policy &amp;amp; National Security end to end: where the opportunity is, how Altana is positioned to win it, which relationships and contract paths get us there, and the team that makes it happen. Success comes from shaping opportunities early, navigating how the government actually buys, and turning long-term agency bets into won programs — building a durable book of business over time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll be the senior Altana relationship for the agency decision-makers who matter, acting as a thought partner who helps them move through technology transformation. You&#39;ll partner closely with the VP of Global Public Sector, Government Affairs, Capture, Product, Delivery and Implementation, Marketing, Finance/Accounting, and executive leadership. For the right operator, this is some of the most ambitious and rewarding work of a career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Altana&#39;s revenue growth for the Policy &amp;amp; National Security vertical— carry the number, and translate strategy into a concrete plan and a focused set of high-value target agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a field of sellers and own their pipeline and forecast, pursuing complex, large-scale government opportunities that reflect strategic vision and long-term agency bets — with honest rigor about what&#39;s real, what&#39;s at risk, and what it will take to land.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own the Policy &amp;amp; National Security pipeline and forecast, pursuing complex, large-scale government opportunities that reflect strategic vision and long-term agency bets — with honest rigor about what&#39;s real, what&#39;s at risk, and what it will take to land.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape new opportunities by communicating Altana&#39;s value to senior government stakeholders and partnering with them as they design their transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop relationships across agencies, from the operational level to the strategic, and build the trusted standing that keeps opening the next opportunity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the partner relationships that extend the vertical&#39;s reach — systems integrators, primes, teaming partners — activating Altana&#39;s broader network to open doors, shape opportunities, and win programs together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside the other GPS leaders to position Altana across the full set of company-wide objectives, so the verticals add up to more than the sum of their parts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate what each pursuit will require and surface those needs internally early, coordinating across teams you don&#39;t directly control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed Policy &amp;amp; National Security signal — budget cycles, policy shifts, competitive intel, real agency needs — into Product, pricing, and company strategy, and own the personas and mission outcomes that help drive the product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in public-sector sales and revenue growth leadership, with a track record of growing the pipeline and the team..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of how the public sector actually buys: you&#39;ve shaped opportunities and made real calls on deal strategies with an understanding of different contracting mechanisms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A network across government and industry you can activate, and the credibility to operate at the senior level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder&#39;s instinct: you&#39;ve led complex efforts, you operate effectively through influence, and you&#39;re energized by standing up something new.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to carry complex, high-intellectual-content software into government; fluency in trade, supply chains, geopolitics, and national security use cases is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent judgment and communication skills, with the ability to engage senior stakeholders independently and translate complex value into a clear case.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The patience and optimism to prevail in long government procurement cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligibility to obtain and hold a U.S. Security Clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in New York, Washington, DC, or London, UK with hybrid work flexibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UK Salary Range&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;£130,000 - £155,000 GBP&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Salary Range and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$200,000 - $250,000 USD&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The salary range, to the extent specified for this role, is a good faith statement of the minimum and maximum levels of the annual based salary for the position.&amp;nbsp; The base salary offered to a successful candidate will depend on a wide range of compensation factors, including, but not limited to, work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Altana&#39;s total compensation package. Altana also offers either a discretionary bonus or a variable compensation plan depending on the role. Additionally, Altana offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Time Off: Altana operates with a Flexible Time Oﬀ (FTO) policy that gives you agency over your own time oﬀ so you can maximize your work-life balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave: We oﬀer industry leading Paid Parental Leave (PPL), providing 14 weeks of leave for non-birthing, adoptive, and foster parents and up to 26 weeks of leave for birthing parents, all paid at 100% of your base salary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Benefits: We have a full suite of medical, vision, and dental benefits with generous employer contributions, designed to give you flexibility and choice for your individual health situation. Our high deductible health plan is 100% employer paid for employees and supplemented with an employer contribution to your Health Savings Account (HSA). There is also a Flexible Spending Account (FSA) option.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supplemental Benefits: Altana provides life, short- and long-term disability, and AD&amp;amp;D insurance coverage, all at no cost to you, so you know that you and your loved ones are covered in case of an emergency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) Savings: Save for and invest in your future using our Fidelity 401(k) retirement savings program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter Benefits: Save money on your commute by setting aside pre-tax funds for public transit or parking!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness: Because we value mental and emotional health, every Altana employee has access to a free premium subscription to Calm, the #1 app for meditation, sleep, and mindfulness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pet Insurance: Pets are family too! Keep them healthy with Wishbone insurance and / or our Total Pet vet service and telehealth discount plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program: Free access to confidential personal support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dependent Care FSA: You will have access to a Dependent Care FSA, which allows you to set aside pre-tax funds for childcare expenses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recruiter assigned to this role can share more information about the specific compensation and benefit details associated with this role during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our values are the core beliefs that shape who we are, what we stand for, and how we behave.They form the foundation of Altana’s culture and integrity and guide how we hire, design, build, and connect with each other and our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trust:&lt;/strong&gt; Our customers and partners entrust us with missions of the highest importance. We honor that by keeping our word, meeting commitments, and ensuring every action we take reinforces confidence in us. We rely on each other to deliver, to speak openly, and to hold ourselves accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resilience: &lt;/strong&gt;In a world of uncertainty and complexity, our work must withstand challenges, evolve with conditions, and ensure reliability over time. Resilience is both how we operate and what we deliver. It’s how we respond when things don’t go to plan –– we adapt, we support each other, and we keep moving forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stewardship:&lt;/strong&gt; We are stewards of every mission we touch. Because our work impacts lives and futures, we hold ourselves accountable to delivering mission impact and never compromising. Our responsibility extends beyond individual projects to the broader system of global trade. We believe that stewardship starts from within so that we can bring focus, creativity, and excellence to our work. Each of us is personally responsible for fostering a workplace where people can thrive. And we are stewards of the greater good of the company. By holding ourselves and each other accountable, we build a culture of innovation and collective success that reflects the scale of our mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Courage: &lt;/strong&gt;Courage is what unlocks the seemingly impossible for our customers. It’s the core value that drives us make bold moves and take on big, complicated network problems—the ones others avoid. We know success isn&#39;t guaranteed, but we have the audacious vision to believe a solution is possible and to build it. Courage fuels our growth mindset. It means embracing challenges that make us stronger, and it’s demonstrated by how we approach hard conversations and complex projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
