&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/firmus/principal-engineer-platform-sydney-australia-409539","tags":["Platform Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Sydney, Australia","created_at":1792346129},{"slug":"ux-copywriter-london-145530","company_name":"Zilch","title":"UX Copywriter","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we are:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're one of Europe's fastest-growing fintech companies – on a mission to create the world's most empowering way to pay.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched the product in 2020 and achieved double unicorn status, valued at $2 billion, and since then have taken on more than 6 million customers.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission is to become the best way to pay for anything, anywhere and say goodbye to credit costs for everyone. This is huge. Want to join us?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We’re looking for a UX copywriter to join our copy team and help bring the Zilch brand to life across every digital customer touchpoint.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your primary focus will be partnering with Product Design to create clear and intuitive experiences across our app and website. Working closely with product designers, product managers and engineers, you'll contribute to creating customer journeys from discovery through to launch.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also collaborate with teams across the business, including Marketing, Customer Support and Operations, providing specialist copy support wherever it's needed – from SEO content and help articles to customer communications and product launches.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This isn't just about writing functional copy. It's about creating experiences customers understand, trust and enjoy. You'll know when to keep things simple, when to inject personality and how to bring the Zilch tone of voice to life in even the smallest moments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a creative and tactical thinker who understands that great UX copy does more than guide users from A to B. It solves problems, removes friction and creates experiences that feel simple, human and unmistakably Zilch.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Day to day responsibilities.</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product Design to create clear, engaging copy across the app and website, from new features to end-to-end customer journeys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with product managers, designers and engineers throughout the product development process, from discovery through to launch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and optimise customer-facing content across digital touchpoints, including help articles, FAQs, SEO content and operational communications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Balance customer needs, business goals and regulatory requirements to create content that's clear, helpful and compliant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use customer insight, data and testing to improve the content and customer journeys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion accessibility, consistency and best practice in UX writing and content design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support wider business priorities with copy for product launches, campaigns and new initiatives when needed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for...</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're a brilliant writer with experience creating content for digital products. Whether you've called yourself a UX Writer, Content Designer or Copywriter, you know how to use words to solve problems. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can switch effectively between product thinking and brand thinking. One minute you're refining onboarding copy, the next you're shaping a product launch or crafting a headline that makes someone smile. </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You know that the best digital experiences don't happen by accident. You're curious, ask the right questions and enjoy getting to the root of a problem before putting pen to paper. </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You care about craft. Every word has a purpose, every interaction has intent and you're never afraid to rewrite something until it feels just right. </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand our tone of voice and apply it consistently across customer communications, recognising how a brand comes to life through product. You know how to create experiences that feel consistent, human and unmistakably Zilch. </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're a natural collaborator who enjoys bouncing ideas around with designers, product managers, marketers and developers. You know the best work happens when different disciplines come together. </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable working in a fast-moving environment where priorities evolve, and you enjoy the variety that comes with it. </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Figma is important. Experience writing for SEO or in a regulated industry would be a bonus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />Compensation &amp; Savings:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Death in Service scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Income Protection.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Permanent employees enjoy access to our Share Options Scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5% back on in-app purchases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">£200 for WFH Setup.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health &amp; Wellbeing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private Medical Insurance including;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">GP consultations (video, telephone or face-to-face).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prescribed medication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In-patient, day-patient and out-patient care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental health support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optical, dental &amp; audiological cover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Physiotherapy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced cancer cover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Menopause support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee Assistance Programme including:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited mental health sessions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">24/7 remote GP &amp; physiotherapy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">24/7 helpline for emotional &amp; practical support.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Savings &amp; discounts on everyday shopping.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1:1 personalised well-being consultations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gym membership discounts.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Family Friendly Policies:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced maternity pay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced paternity pay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced adoption pay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced shared parental leave.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; Development:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional Qualifications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional Memberships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning Suite for e-courses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Internal Training Programmes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">FCA &amp; Regulatory training.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Workplace Perks:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid working: office-based Monday, Wednesday, and Thursday; remote working Tuesday and Friday</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Casual dress code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Workplace socials.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healthy snacks.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/zilch/ux-copywriter-london-145530","tags":["Marketing & Design"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zilch UK","created_at":1792345219},{"slug":"finance-manager-london-63756","company_name":"Happl","title":"Finance Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We’re building the next generation of employee benefits infrastructure.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Happl, we help global teams design, manage, and scale benefits that actually work for their people by using AI, across flex allowances, benefits, insurance, recognition, and wellbeing, all in one intelligent platform.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Happl is backed by leading investors such as <strong>YCombinator, 6Degrees Capital, Haatch,</strong> <strong>Portage</strong>, and more, known for backing leading companies such as <strong>Deel, Rippling, Airbnb, Coinbase, Dropbox</strong>, and most recently was awarded a place in the <strong>UK’s top 100 startups for 2026</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Financial Controller at Happl, you’ll own the financial engine of the business — everything from the cash in the bank to the numbers our board and investors use to make decisions runs through you. You’ll run the monthly close, the full revenue cycle, the compliance calendar across two jurisdictions, and our treasury position, and you’ll decide how all of it gets built, systemised, and automated.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on, high-autonomy role with a direct line to leadership. You won’t be managing a process someone else designed — you’ll be deciding what good looks like across revenue, cash, compliance, and reporting, then making it happen. You’ll work closely with the CEO, the board, our investors, and our outsourced bookkeeping, audit, and tax partners, holding all of it to a standard that matches the product we’ve built.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re FCA-regulated and YCombinator-backed, having raised $11m to date, and we give global employers a single place to design, deliver, and manage benefits across 160+ countries and 70+ languages — which means the finance function behind the product has to be just as sharp as the product itself. We’re entering our next phase of growth, with an ambitious revenue trajectory and an expanding international footprint, and this role sits at the centre of it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owning the monthly close on a fixed timetable</strong> — management accounts, balance sheet integrity, accruals, prepayments, and the revenue and cost reconciliations that sit behind them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Writing the commentary</strong> that explains what’s actually happened in the business, not just what the numbers say</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Producing the monthly investor reporting pack</strong> and the financial sections of board materials — ARR and revenue analysis, cash and runway, burn efficiency, unit economics, cohort and retention metrics, and budget versus actual</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owning the full revenue cycle</strong> — invoicing, collections, aged debt, and revenue recognition across a multi-currency, multi-contract subscription base</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leading the rollout of automated billing</strong> and revenue recognition tooling, moving us from manual tracking to a system that scales without adding headcount</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Managing our two legal entities</strong> — a US TopCo and a UK operating company — including statutory accounts, audit preparation, intercompany accounting, transfer pricing mechanics, and FX exposure between them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owning the compliance calendar end to end</strong> across both jurisdictions — UK VAT returns, corporation tax, US federal and state filings, sales tax where applicable, and payroll taxes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Supporting our FCA regulatory reporting obligations</strong> and the financial controls that sit behind them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Running monthly payroll across jurisdictions</strong>, pension and benefits administration, employee expenses, and the finance side of onboarding and offboarding</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owning the cash position and treasury strategy</strong> — cash flow forecasting, working capital, FX management, and structuring how we hold company funds to earn a sensible return without taking risk we shouldn’t</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Managing our outsourced bookkeeping</strong>, accounting, and tax partners — holding them to deadlines and quality, and pulling work in-house where doing so makes us faster</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owning the finance tech stack and having a strong opinion on it</strong>, actively replacing manual work with automation and AI-assisted workflows across reconciliations, invoice processing, variance analysis, and reporting drafts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leveraging AI tools like Claude and ChatGPT</strong> to speed up your own work and build the systems that let finance scale without adding headcount</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Acting as the financial conscience of the business</strong>, with a direct line to the founders and a real say in how we grow</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualified accountant (ACA, ACCA or CIMA), or qualified by experience with a track record that stands up to scrutiny</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine ownership of a monthly close cycle and management reporting pack, start to finish</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical grounding in revenue recognition, accruals accounting, and balance sheet control</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with tax and compliance across VAT, corporation tax, and payroll, ideally spanning both the UK and US</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI-native in your approach — you already use AI tools in your day-to-day work and can talk specifically about what you’ve automated and what it saved you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional attention to detail, alongside the judgement to know when precision matters and when speed does</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear communicator — you can explain a number to a non-finance audience without patronising them or losing them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ideally, SaaS or subscription business experience, particularly ARR reporting and deferred revenue, and familiarity with modern billing infrastructure like Xero or Stripe</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with SQL, Python, or low-code automation tools is a bonus, not a requirement, but it will make your life here significantly easier</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What to expect</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Being Financial Controller at Happl is not a maintenance role. You’ll be building the finance function as you run it — choosing the systems, designing the controls, and deciding how billing, revenue recognition, and reporting should work as we scale into new markets and currencies. That’s not a caveat; it’s the role.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some weeks will be genuinely rewarding — a reporting pack you built gives the board real clarity, a manual process you automated saves the team hours every month, a treasury decision you made puts real value on the table. Some will be hard — closing the books on a fixed timetable, holding partners and advisors to a deadline, and making judgement calls across two jurisdictions with incomplete information.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What you get in return is real scope. You’ll own the whole picture — revenue, cash, compliance, treasury, and reporting — across two jurisdictions and 160+ countries of operations, with a direct line to the founders and reporting that goes straight to the board and our investors. This is the foundation of a finance function that will grow with the business, and the right person grows with it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why join Happl</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of building something that genuinely matters — the future of how companies support their people</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary that reflects the impact you’ll have</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real equity — a meaningful stake in what we’re building together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid working from day one, with the trust and flexibility to do your best work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your own Happl account — use the platform you’re helping to build and shape</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private Health Insurance, because we genuinely care about how you’re doing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dental insurance, including family cover</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A personal Wellbeing budget to spend however wellbeing works for you — no questions asked</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A dedicated L&amp;D budget to grow in the direction that excites you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension — we’re invested in your future, not just the short term</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Interview</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 1: 20-min Intro call with Ben Shorrock (Head of Operations)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 2: Short task</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage 3: 30-min deep dive and task review with Ben T (CEO) &amp; Ben S (Ops)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Additional Details</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Location: London, Holborn</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team: Finance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reports to: CEO</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working arrangement: Hybrid (4+ Days in Office)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#BS-L1</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/happl/finance-manager-london-63756","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792345218},{"slug":"growth-analyst-london-440340","company_name":"Goodlord","title":"Growth Analyst","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">📍<strong>Location - this role is based in our London office 2 days per week with the remaining 3 days working remotely</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Business to Consumer Partnerships is one of the most entrepreneurial teams at Goodlord, and we’re looking for a Growth Analyst to join us!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is all about spotting growth opportunities and making them happen. You’ll look at where we can improve broadband and media conversion, unlock the potential of smaller partnerships and build propositions for under-served tenant groups.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll have real ownership from day one, using data, commercial thinking and great relationships to turn ideas into action. As the team grows, there’s a clear opportunity to take ownership of your own product vertical too.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Opportunity:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use data and insight to identify commercial opportunities and drive improvements in partner conversion and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain dashboards, forecasting models and trend analysis to give the team clear visibility and support decision-making.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own relationships with smaller partners, identifying, testing and developing new commercial opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work cross-functionally with Partnerships, Finance, Product and Commercial teams to develop propositions and improve the tenant journey.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we need from you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a commercial, partnerships, analytics or growth-focused role, with a strong track record of spotting and pursuing opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A natural relationship-builder who is confident working with external partners, presenting insights and challenging internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly organised and proactive, with the drive to take ownership, turn ideas into action and see them through to completion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong data and Excel/Google Sheets skills, with the ability to build models and dashboards and turn insights into clear commercial recommendations.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>It would also be great if:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have an interest in the tenant experience, renting or PropTech.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve worked in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re confident presenting commercial ideas and backing up your thinking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience with SQL or BI tools.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our mission:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two in five people in the UK rent their homes. Goodlord's mission? To be the gold standard platform for renting 🌎</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We started Goodlord because we wanted to make renting simple and transparent for everyone involved: the agent, the landlord, and the tenant. We knew Generation Rent would lead to more tenants, with higher digital expectations and we were confident we could provide a solution 🏠</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Like all scale-ups it’s been a bit of a rollercoaster journey, but we’re now stronger than ever, with around 3,000 letting agents using the platform, exciting and varied products and 350+ Goodlordians across the group supporting the mission! 💚</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why you'll love being a Goodlordian</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aside from the role, the people, our culture and our mission, we have some other things that make Goodlord a pretty awesome place to be. Here’s a few favourites amongst Goodlordians (check out our careers page for more info).</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow with Goodlord:</strong> your development is important to us, that’s why we are <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.greatplacetowork.co.uk/certified-company/1558877">Great Place to Work - certified</a>. Have a goal in mind? Share it with us so we can use some of our annual development fund to support it. We guarantee you’ll learn loads and develop both personally and professionally!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your well-being matters:</strong> bi-weekly coaching with Sanctus to provide Goodlordians with a safe place to talk and support your mental health</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>25 days holiday (plus UK Bank holidays) plus 1 day per full holiday year up to 32 days:</strong> We believe regular breaks are essential for well-being and we encourage (some may say expect!) all Goodlordians to take full advantage of their annual leave entitlement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Supporting your family:</strong> we offer Goodlordians of all genders a generous 3 months of fully-paid time off to look after their new arrivals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our team:</strong> we’re an energetic, sociable, and talented bunch who are super passionate about what we do and determined to make a difference. We’re all in it together, we learn from each other, we’re genuine and we don’t have time for politics</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What’s next?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re ready to help us on our mission to be the gold standard platform for renting, then click apply (2-3 minutes)!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A full job spec is available on request.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Goodlord wants applicants from all backgrounds and walks of life; we are an equal opportunity employer committed to creating an inclusive environment. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creating a space where everyone feels included is central to who we are. Because we're an open book and we learn from each other, we actively champion diverse perspectives and unique life experiences. If there is anything you need to participate fully in the interview process, we'd love to hear about that too - please include it in your application.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />** Please note, as we are regulated by the Financial Conduct Authority, all Goodlordians are required to pass a thorough referencing check via Experian before joining the team. We will only ask for references at the point of making an offer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>No agencies please</strong> - we have tried and trusted partners we would turn to should we require support.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/goodlord/growth-analyst-london-440340","tags":["B2C Partnerships"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792345217},{"slug":"customer-success-manager-emea-london-68557","company_name":"Notabene","title":"Customer Success Manager, EMEA","description":"<h3><strong>About Notabene</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notabene is building infrastructure that’s transforming how money moves in t