 that adapt to any environment or use case. We’ve already achieved what many thought impossible: the world’s most advanced GNSS chipset. But that’s just the beginning.</p><p class="MsoNormal">At Qualinx, we believe that the future of connectivity lies in precision, efficiency, and adaptability. Our ambition is to become the invisible thread that seamlessly interconnects billions of devices: powering a smarter, more responsive world.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What Sets Us Apart</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">Joining Qualinx is about becoming part of a culture that’s as ambitious as it is authentic. We hold ourselves to high standards, thrive on solving the unexpected, and push boundaries together. But we also know how to enjoy the ride. Our culture is a unique blend of curiosity, team spirit, and a touch of unconventional charm. It’s fast-paced, fun, and grounded in a sober sense of purpose and perspective. Whether we’re deep in design reviews or sharing laughs over lunch, we’re building something meaningful together. At Qualinx, you’re not just contributing to a ground-breaking technology, you’re helping shape a team that’s redefining what it means to work in deep tech.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW41210993 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW41210993 BCX8"><strong>Job Description</strong>&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align:start;">As a Test Engineer, you will support the development and production release of test solutions for Qualinx products. Working closely with Design, Product Engineering, Reliability, and external manufacturing partners, you will contribute to digital and memory test development activities, product characterization, yield improvement, and production support.</p><p style="text-align:start;">&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul><li><p>Support the development, validation, and release of production test solutions for Qualinx products.</p></li><li><p>Support in developing and debugging ATE test programs for wafer sort and final test.</p></li><li><p>Support silicon characterization, correlation, and production qualification activities.</p></li><li><p>Analyze test results and production data to identify issues and opportunities for yield improvement.</p></li><li><p>Work with Design and Product Engineering teams to investigate test failures and support root cause analysis.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to test time optimization and test coverage improvements.</p></li><li><p>Support OSAT and manufacturing partners during product bring-up and production ramp.</p></li><li><p>Assist in implementing and validating digital test methodologies, including SCAN, MBIST, JTAG, and Flash testing.</p></li><li><p>Develop automation scripts and tools to improve test efficiency and data analysis.</p></li><li><p>Maintain test documentation and support continuous improvement of test processes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li><p>Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering, Electronics Engineering, Semiconductor Engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p>Minimum five years of experience in semiconductor test engineering, product engineering, or a related role.</p></li><li><p>Semiconductor test development and production test flow experience.</p></li><li><p>Experience with semiconductor testing at wafer sort and/or package level.</p></li><li><p>Experience with embedded digital interfaces such as SPI, I2C, UART, SWD, and JTAG.</p></li><li><p>Understanding of digital test methodologies, including SCAN, MBIST, JTAG/Boundary Scan, IDDQ and Flash Memory Testing</p></li><li><p>Experience with ATE platforms or test development environments such as NI and Teradyne IG-XL.</p></li><li><p>Programming or scripting experience in Python, C/C++, MATLAB, or similar languages.</p></li><li><p>Understanding of electronics fundamentals and digital circuit operation.</p></li><li><p>Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p>Good communication skills and the ability to work effectively in a diverse cross-functional team.</p></li><li><p>Experience with NI PXIe, Teradyne J750HD, or UltraFLEX platforms.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;">&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Preferred Experience</strong></p><ul><li><p>Familiarity with data analysis tools (e.g MATLAB, JMP, or equivalent).</p></li><li><p>Experience with ATPG and vector conversion flows using tools for production ATE implementation.</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of Design-for-Test (DFT) concepts, including Scan, MBIST, JTAG, Boundary Scan, and ATPG.</p></li><li><p>Experience working with OSATs in NPI and high-volume manufacturing environments.</p></li><li><p>Exposure to WLCSP products, wafer sort, and wafer-level development and testing methodologies.</p></li><li><p>Experience with test data analysis and yield monitoring tools is preferred.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What's in it for you?</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">At Qualinx, we believe that great work starts with a great environment, pioneering technology and a fun dynamic market to address. Here’s what you can expect when you join our team:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Ownership and Impact</strong>: We offer employee equity, giving you the opportunity to share in the success you help create.</p></li><li><p><strong>Well-being Matters</strong>: Your physical and mental health are important to us. We provide access to wellness resources, including company discounts and a free mental healthcare platform.</p></li><li><p><strong>Global Talent, Local Support</strong>: If you're relocating from abroad, we provide full support throughout the visa process to ensure a smooth transition.</p></li><li><p><strong>Future-Focused Benefits</strong>: We contribute to your pension savings to help you plan ahead with confidence.<